WEBVTT

1
00:01:35.502 --> 00:01:37.202
Crazy bastards!

2
00:02:30.662 --> 00:02:33.422
Is there a place
without any worries?

3
00:02:33.732 --> 00:02:36.892
If such a place existed,
we'd want to go there now.

4
00:02:38.332 --> 00:02:41.671
Maybe that's what Dorothy
in 'Wizard of Oz' was thinking

5
00:02:41.672 --> 00:02:44.402
when she dreamed of a world
beyond the rainbow.

6
00:02:45.172 --> 00:02:50.082
Wouldn't it be great if we could
go to the place of our dreams

7
00:02:50.312 --> 00:02:54.412
by clicking our heels three
times with our eyes closed?

8
00:02:56.452 --> 00:02:58.902
Going beyond the rainbow.

9
00:02:58.922 --> 00:03:03.802
At first, it's a new and
scary thing for everyone.

10
00:03:03.892 --> 00:03:09.121
But, once adjusted, you find
that there's only one place

11
00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:12.122
where you can stay without any worries.

12
00:03:13.332 --> 00:03:14.662
That place is right here.

13
00:03:35.162 --> 00:03:36.802
- Let's get this done quickly.
- Yes, sir!

14
00:03:42.962 --> 00:03:45.592
What are you doing?
Get out.

15
00:03:48.702 --> 00:03:50.732
He's so slow.

16
00:04:04.522 --> 00:04:05.522
Go see.

17
00:04:17.532 --> 00:04:20.562
That's when I first met him.

18
00:04:22.172 --> 00:04:23.172
Get inside.

19
00:04:38.822 --> 00:04:39.822
Move it.

20
00:04:42.322 --> 00:04:43.652
Come on.
Move faster.

21
00:04:55.542 --> 00:04:57.541
Electroshock Therapy

22
00:04:57.542 --> 00:04:58.902
You interested in that room?

23
00:05:08.182 --> 00:05:09.182
Move.

24
00:05:12.422 --> 00:05:14.982
The hell? Bastard, you wanna die?

25
00:05:27.032 --> 00:05:30.262
Dad said I can't get
out of here until death.

26
00:05:30.962 --> 00:05:35.072
I'm not sure whose death
he was talking about.

27
00:05:35.312 --> 00:05:37.782
But, this time, I think
he sent me pretty far away.

28
00:05:40.502 --> 00:05:42.921
Since I'm already missing home.

29
00:05:42.922 --> 00:05:44.652
I didn't do anything.

30
00:05:46.122 --> 00:05:48.992
Let me go! Let go!
Let me go!

31
00:05:51.732 --> 00:05:55.792
SHOOT ME IN THE HEART

32
00:05:59.472 --> 00:06:01.872
Mr. LEE Soo-myung.
Try opening your eyes.

33
00:06:04.872 --> 00:06:07.742
- Came in with RYU Seung-min?
- Yes.

34
00:06:07.872 --> 00:06:09.212
Why's he still like this?

35
00:06:10.442 --> 00:06:12.881
When Seung-min was
making a commotion,

36
00:06:12.882 --> 00:06:15.212
the security team gave him
haloperidol by mistake.

37
00:06:16.922 --> 00:06:18.112
As a schizophrenic,

38
00:06:18.182 --> 00:06:20.181
he has auditory hallucination
and panic disorder.

39
00:06:20.182 --> 00:06:22.902
He was released from Rothem
hospital a month ago.

40
00:06:23.092 --> 00:06:24.768
He's back here after
getting into some trouble.

41
00:06:24.792 --> 00:06:28.922
I don't hear things any more.
It stopped 6 months ago.

42
00:06:30.432 --> 00:06:31.622
Send him to the ward.

43
00:06:31.732 --> 00:06:33.862
- Tidy up his hair, too.
- Yes, sir.

44
00:06:40.842 --> 00:06:42.712
Hey, schizo!

45
00:06:47.652 --> 00:06:49.052
Never been to the army, right?

46
00:06:50.552 --> 00:06:52.392
Well, they won't accept
crazy ones like you.

47
00:06:52.622 --> 00:06:53.882
Listen carefully.

48
00:06:54.152 --> 00:06:57.252
Nobody's here to pamper you
like at Rothem.

49
00:06:57.322 --> 00:07:01.522
So, think you're in the army
and move fast. Or you die.

50
00:07:06.232 --> 00:07:09.362
Get up now! Get out, you creep!

51
00:07:16.382 --> 00:07:18.342
I told you not to use English!

52
00:07:21.822 --> 00:07:25.552
"Nurse CHOl Ki-hoon is
sexually intimate with dogs."

53
00:07:25.892 --> 00:07:28.152
if I say that in Korean,
you'll get mad.

54
00:07:28.252 --> 00:07:31.522
RYU Seung-min,
do you remember this guy?

55
00:07:31.832 --> 00:07:33.852
He saw blood because of you
the other night.

56
00:07:33.962 --> 00:07:35.432
His name is LEE Soo-myung.

57
00:07:38.602 --> 00:07:39.602
Hi.

58
00:07:42.572 --> 00:07:44.772
First time seeing a crazy one?
You crazy bastard.

59
00:07:44.902 --> 00:07:47.272
Throw another fit and I'll just!

60
00:07:50.672 --> 00:07:53.272
What a pity we meet in
this shit hole, baby.

61
00:07:53.282 --> 00:07:54.642
What are you doing?

62
00:08:02.862 --> 00:08:03.862
Go, now.

63
00:08:04.592 --> 00:08:05.822
Move it!

64
00:08:12.802 --> 00:08:16.921
Now, these are the hospital rules.

65
00:08:16.922 --> 00:08:19.021
Wake up at 6:30AM. Go to sleep at 10PM.

66
00:08:19.022 --> 00:08:22.021
No going out during sleeping hours.

67
00:08:22.022 --> 00:08:25.922
In emergencies, press the
red button by the door.

68
00:08:26.452 --> 00:08:28.712
Private calls to outside are
absolutely prohibited.

69
00:08:29.082 --> 00:08:31.022
If we catch you "flying pigeons",

70
00:08:31.552 --> 00:08:34.491
- you'll be in isolation for 3 days.
- What bullshit!

71
00:08:34.492 --> 00:08:36.112
It's urgent.
I have to call.

72
00:08:36.222 --> 00:08:39.712
Fill in the call request form and
hand it in the nurse room.

73
00:08:39.992 --> 00:08:41.161
We'll call for you
after evaluating it.

74
00:08:41.162 --> 00:08:42.992
Evaluate and call for me?

75
00:08:43.602 --> 00:08:45.332
Why do you do that?

76
00:08:45.432 --> 00:08:48.232
Is this some kind of a prison?
Fuck!

77
00:08:55.412 --> 00:08:58.832
Absolutely no alcohol. Smoke
only in the smoking room.

78
00:08:59.712 --> 00:09:01.342
The personal items we give you,

79
00:09:01.412 --> 00:09:03.312
take care not to get them stolen.

80
00:09:03.622 --> 00:09:05.112
By policy,

81
00:09:06.492 --> 00:09:08.182
we'd have to take your watch, too.

82
00:09:08.492 --> 00:09:09.961
We'll let you keep it
since it's not metal.

83
00:09:09.962 --> 00:09:12.661
I have to use the phone.
Right now.

84
00:09:12.662 --> 00:09:14.351
I told you after 2 weeks.

85
00:09:14.352 --> 00:09:17.152
Whether you make the call
depends on your behavior.

86
00:09:17.562 --> 00:09:21.562
Your behavior right now is D-.

87
00:09:22.402 --> 00:09:25.001
Can't you hear what I'm saying?

88
00:09:25.002 --> 00:09:29.062
One phone call and I've got
no business seeing you guys.

89
00:09:29.762 --> 00:09:31.792
Do I look the same as these people?

90
00:09:45.262 --> 00:09:48.192
Try not to cause any trouble
like the other night.

91
00:09:49.432 --> 00:09:51.522
We're letting you off
since it's your first time.

92
00:09:55.842 --> 00:09:59.132
You'll get a haircut soon.
Come out when we call you.

93
00:10:03.812 --> 00:10:06.572
No, no haircut for me.
No haircut.

94
00:10:07.782 --> 00:10:08.972
Fuck!

95
00:10:20.332 --> 00:10:23.162
Came to the psych ward
instead of the eye doctor.

96
00:10:24.262 --> 00:10:25.392
Isn't it unfair?

97
00:10:25.832 --> 00:10:29.602
I've seen so many who's been
dragged in here unfairly.

98
00:10:29.872 --> 00:10:31.911
But, before you leave,

99
00:10:31.912 --> 00:10:34.432
have a look around.
When could you even come in here?

100
00:10:34.772 --> 00:10:37.262
Now, I'll show you around.

101
00:10:37.812 --> 00:10:39.972
This here is a race walker.

102
00:10:39.982 --> 00:10:43.442
In 1 year, he walks as much as
traveling the whole country.

103
00:10:43.452 --> 00:10:46.852
The only couple in our hospital.
Han and Eun.

104
00:10:46.952 --> 00:10:50.052
They hope to be released
when they become legally adults.

105
00:10:50.262 --> 00:10:53.131
This is Hyun-sun's Mom.
So sad.

106
00:10:53.132 --> 00:10:55.662
She keeps looking for
Hyun-sun who died in the fire.

107
00:10:55.762 --> 00:10:59.601
He drank too much outside
and became an alcoholic.

108
00:10:59.602 --> 00:11:01.192
He's improved a lot now.

109
00:11:03.042 --> 00:11:04.271
See that guy looking over here?

110
00:11:04.272 --> 00:11:07.902
He's Mr. Know-It-All.
A.K.A. the Guru.

111
00:11:08.142 --> 00:11:11.672
Can't call his father as father
nor his brother as brother.

112
00:11:12.072 --> 00:11:15.772
Born naked, only to take
one pair of clothes! Amen.

113
00:11:16.852 --> 00:11:17.942
What's he talking about?

114
00:11:18.182 --> 00:11:19.251
Oh, Buddhist Goddess of Mercy...

115
00:11:19.252 --> 00:11:21.312
The last person to introduce is...

116
00:11:23.662 --> 00:11:27.082
Ah, over there. He plays
the harmonica really well.

117
00:11:27.092 --> 00:11:29.802
People call him the street
musician and like him a lot.

118
00:11:29.812 --> 00:11:31.842
But after a few shock therapies...

119
00:11:33.172 --> 00:11:34.471
he attained enlightenment.

120
00:11:34.472 --> 00:11:38.472
Now he can't recognize his
own mother or the harmonica.

121
00:11:38.972 --> 00:11:39.972
Hey!

122
00:11:42.842 --> 00:11:45.442
That guy is the hospital director's nephew.

123
00:11:45.582 --> 00:11:46.851
He's a bit slow.

124
00:11:46.852 --> 00:11:51.042
So, he's the type who
can't work a desk job.

125
00:11:51.382 --> 00:11:53.512
You want to die?

126
00:11:54.212 --> 00:11:57.312
Where'd you get that gown? Take it off now!

127
00:12:05.832 --> 00:12:06.832
What the...?

128
00:12:09.422 --> 00:12:12.962
You had your baby's first birthday party?
What did he pick for his future job?

129
00:12:12.972 --> 00:12:14.602
Probably a bat,
just like his Dad?

130
00:12:14.672 --> 00:12:16.732
Let's get along well together!
We're roommates!

131
00:12:16.812 --> 00:12:18.042
You bastard!

132
00:12:20.482 --> 00:12:21.482
What the...?

133
00:12:37.162 --> 00:12:40.692
Huh?
What's going on?

134
00:12:55.192 --> 00:12:56.992
What's going on?

135
00:13:06.402 --> 00:13:09.002
What are you doing there? Come out now!

136
00:13:09.862 --> 00:13:13.332
Come out. Come out. Come out. Come out!

137
00:13:15.802 --> 00:13:17.002
Need more beating?

138
00:13:21.472 --> 00:13:22.632
Fuck!

139
00:13:33.522 --> 00:13:34.522
You're dead!

140
00:13:36.992 --> 00:13:38.222
You bastard!

141
00:13:45.502 --> 00:13:48.332
Hey! Stop right there!
Stop!

142
00:14:02.102 --> 00:14:04.651
No, no. We weren't going to escape.

143
00:14:04.652 --> 00:14:06.912
I asked to use his phone
but he just attacked me.

144
00:14:07.712 --> 00:14:09.712
Hey! What's the password?

145
00:14:10.412 --> 00:14:12.312
This asshole's locked the phone.

146
00:14:14.352 --> 00:14:16.712
Let me just use the phone once!

147
00:14:17.232 --> 00:14:18.892
Just one call!

148
00:14:26.472 --> 00:14:27.902
Let's first cut the hair.

149
00:14:28.502 --> 00:14:30.602
Then you're both dead.

150
00:14:32.302 --> 00:14:33.802
You come here.

151
00:14:39.292 --> 00:14:40.292
Where you going?

152
00:14:41.752 --> 00:14:43.282
- Hold him.
- Yes, sir.

153
00:14:46.032 --> 00:14:47.152
It'll be over soon.

154
00:14:48.362 --> 00:14:49.452
Stay still.

155
00:14:55.952 --> 00:14:58.152
Shut up, you creep!

156
00:14:59.442 --> 00:15:00.532
This is no use.

157
00:15:04.532 --> 00:15:05.632
Stay still.

158
00:15:16.092 --> 00:15:17.562
Fuck! You bastard!

159
00:15:17.722 --> 00:15:19.322
Take the crazy fuck out of here!

160
00:15:20.062 --> 00:15:21.992
Why's he always fucking with me?

161
00:15:35.142 --> 00:15:36.442
SHILLIM BOOKSTORE

162
00:15:50.422 --> 00:15:52.412
Your father sent the documents.

163
00:15:52.562 --> 00:15:56.012
You don't have to get a haircut
because you have scissor phobia.

164
00:15:56.032 --> 00:15:58.902
Instead, always wear a hat.

165
00:16:09.182 --> 00:16:11.172
Hyun-sun.

166
00:16:12.612 --> 00:16:14.842
Hyun-sun.

167
00:16:40.102 --> 00:16:43.241
Miss Lee.
Miss Lee?~

168
00:16:43.242 --> 00:16:45.142
Do you dig me, baby?

169
00:16:48.012 --> 00:16:51.782
Since I'm not sleepy,
should we go on a date?

170
00:16:54.022 --> 00:16:55.252
Crazy bastard!

171
00:17:33.732 --> 00:17:35.331
Wake up! Wake up!

172
00:17:35.332 --> 00:17:37.332
What is this?

173
00:17:39.102 --> 00:17:44.202
You two! Why are you
hugging there like that? Ah, you nut-jobs.

174
00:17:56.462 --> 00:17:58.462
Ddobyul.

175
00:18:02.462 --> 00:18:03.462
Ddobyul!

176
00:18:03.862 --> 00:18:05.692
What's this?

177
00:18:05.932 --> 00:18:08.631
Man-sik handled
horses at the circus.

178
00:18:08.632 --> 00:18:10.161
His favorite horse was
named Ddobyul.

179
00:18:10.162 --> 00:18:13.352
Man-sik lost it when he died.

180
00:18:13.432 --> 00:18:14.592
Get off!

181
00:18:15.292 --> 00:18:18.192
Congrats on becoming the 16th Ddobyul.

182
00:18:18.202 --> 00:18:21.542
Ah, shit. Let go of me.
Get off of me!

183
00:18:42.832 --> 00:18:44.162
ART THERAPY

184
00:18:59.412 --> 00:19:00.542
Stay still.

185
00:19:08.192 --> 00:19:10.052
Newbies always stand out.

186
00:19:10.822 --> 00:19:14.422
As if he's the only sane
person, he acts snobbish.

187
00:19:15.062 --> 00:19:17.532
He acts out to get attention.

188
00:19:18.602 --> 00:19:21.401
And, with meaningless actions,

189
00:19:21.402 --> 00:19:23.752
he makes others uncomfortable.

190
00:19:24.102 --> 00:19:25.732
I said "no"!

191
00:19:25.792 --> 00:19:27.931
Why not?

192
00:19:27.932 --> 00:19:30.431
It's policy to fill out the form.

193
00:19:30.432 --> 00:19:32.732
I have to make the call myself!

194
00:19:33.112 --> 00:19:35.741
All these people want to
make the call themselves.

195
00:19:35.742 --> 00:19:37.281
To the dead husband.

196
00:19:37.282 --> 00:19:38.752
The missing daughter.

197
00:19:38.852 --> 00:19:40.792
Even to KiM Jong-il.

198
00:19:42.602 --> 00:19:43.712
You kidding me?

199
00:19:43.722 --> 00:19:44.982
You have two options.

200
00:19:45.192 --> 00:19:46.791
Stand there and stay angry.

201
00:19:46.792 --> 00:19:49.592
Or, fill in the form and go eat.

202
00:19:50.732 --> 00:19:53.792
Ddobyul, let's go eat.

203
00:20:00.642 --> 00:20:01.642
All right.

204
00:20:02.132 --> 00:20:05.432
Then deliver this message.
That I'll make a deal.

205
00:20:05.742 --> 00:20:07.342
They'll understand.

206
00:20:18.422 --> 00:20:19.982
I heard you were a lighter.

207
00:20:20.782 --> 00:20:22.881
Mr. Know-It-All is also a lighter.

208
00:20:22.882 --> 00:20:25.782
He was happy to meet his own kind.

209
00:20:32.282 --> 00:20:34.912
A lighter is a pyromaniac.

210
00:20:35.412 --> 00:20:40.312
People in the ward consider a
lighter as the king of crazies.

211
00:20:40.612 --> 00:20:44.542
They're the real nut-jobs that
even crazies are scared of.

212
00:20:44.552 --> 00:20:47.612
I knew it.
He's such bad news.

213
00:20:49.962 --> 00:20:51.022
Yong.

214
00:20:52.022 --> 00:20:54.022
I got something to ask you.

215
00:20:54.532 --> 00:20:56.352
Why do you ask?

216
00:20:56.702 --> 00:20:59.592
Because something might
happen during the night.

217
00:20:59.602 --> 00:21:05.002
I should know about
what's going on around here.

218
00:21:07.372 --> 00:21:08.342
But, I take sleeping pills.

219
00:21:08.343 --> 00:21:11.472
So, I don't know
what came or went.

220
00:21:12.952 --> 00:21:17.742
But, that guardian who came...
he's not your family, right?

221
00:21:18.782 --> 00:21:21.852
Did you set his house on fire?
On fire?

222
00:21:31.962 --> 00:21:32.962
Thank you!

223
00:21:39.742 --> 00:21:42.032
So, are there always
2 night patrols?

224
00:21:42.042 --> 00:21:43.732
Not always.

225
00:21:43.742 --> 00:21:46.451
Spotty plays cards,
so he never comes.

226
00:21:46.452 --> 00:21:50.382
CHOI Ki-hoon is a loner
so he likes being alone.

227
00:21:56.292 --> 00:21:57.361
Ball, ball, ball.

228
00:21:57.362 --> 00:21:58.722
OK.

229
00:22:06.832 --> 00:22:08.162
Who the fuck was it?

230
00:22:08.572 --> 00:22:09.572
Hey!

231
00:22:11.072 --> 00:22:14.002
- Are you crazy?
- Mr. RYU Seung-min! Visitor!

232
00:22:15.142 --> 00:22:17.042
Visitor. Visitor.

233
00:22:18.802 --> 00:22:21.442
He must finally be getting out.

234
00:22:29.962 --> 00:22:33.792
Now, I had to carry
Man-sik on my back.

235
00:22:36.102 --> 00:22:37.792
VISITOR ROOM

236
00:22:52.952 --> 00:22:56.212
Pick whichever and
leave your name.

237
00:22:56.882 --> 00:23:00.682
So far, I found out this man has 3 jobs.

238
00:23:00.722 --> 00:23:05.052
Laundryman, cleaner, and now a book dealer.

239
00:23:10.352 --> 00:23:12.622
Pencils aren't allowed in here.

240
00:23:13.132 --> 00:23:15.662
Even when we're not
felons, we're just crazy.

241
00:23:17.972 --> 00:23:19.602
First, solve inside the parentheses.

242
00:23:19.712 --> 00:23:22.602
Move the variable to the left.
The constant to the right.

243
00:23:27.902 --> 00:23:31.302
No, first do the transposition.
Transfer.

244
00:23:31.752 --> 00:23:34.812
I was going to do that!
Transfer!

245
00:23:42.292 --> 00:23:47.202
But, how do you do that?
Transfer?

246
00:23:50.042 --> 00:23:54.232
I've never talked so much
since I was 19 years old.

247
00:23:59.012 --> 00:24:01.741
- Give me my clothes and wallet.
- What?

248
00:24:01.742 --> 00:24:04.672
They arranged for me to leave!

249
00:24:05.082 --> 00:24:06.552
I didn't hear about that.

250
00:24:06.652 --> 00:24:08.512
What do you mean?

251
00:24:08.712 --> 00:24:13.182
The guardian will come and
release me on Wednesday.

252
00:24:13.332 --> 00:24:16.801
Look. See the director's signature?

253
00:24:16.802 --> 00:24:17.901
Are you messing with me?

254
00:24:17.902 --> 00:24:20.222
Mr. Ryu Seung-Min, I don't
have the release order.

255
00:24:20.232 --> 00:24:23.001
Forget the order! I'm getting out now.

256
00:24:23.002 --> 00:24:24.501
Ryu Seung-Min.

257
00:24:24.502 --> 00:24:25.602
Follow me.

258
00:24:28.012 --> 00:24:29.032
Yeah, let's talk.

259
00:24:29.542 --> 00:24:31.202
Can't communicate at all.

260
00:24:34.152 --> 00:24:36.082
Visitor Request Form.
I have to...

261
00:24:36.952 --> 00:24:38.582
We don't have any.

262
00:24:39.652 --> 00:24:42.142
How many times did I ask...

263
00:24:44.522 --> 00:24:46.422
Give me (Oppa) a cigarette.

264
00:24:51.202 --> 00:24:52.692
He's in trouble again.

265
00:24:53.572 --> 00:24:54.572
What happened?

266
00:24:54.752 --> 00:24:58.702
Probably can't get out because
his guardian changed his mind.

267
00:24:58.712 --> 00:25:00.742
Lighter will get in trouble if he goes out.

268
00:25:00.912 --> 00:25:04.032
Mr. Know-It-All said
the impulse to set fire,

269
00:25:05.412 --> 00:25:08.012
it's harder than quitting gambling.

270
00:25:11.382 --> 00:25:13.322
Hyun-sun.

271
00:25:33.142 --> 00:25:34.162
Miss LEE.

272
00:25:34.772 --> 00:25:37.972
Stop looking at me (Oppa)
and just go to sleep.

273
00:26:57.862 --> 00:27:00.392
He had trouble seeing in the dark.

274
00:27:00.792 --> 00:27:02.992
As if he had night blindness.

275
00:27:03.302 --> 00:27:06.692
His eyes couldn't function
properly in the dark.

276
00:27:12.872 --> 00:27:15.642
What could be used as a weapon here?

277
00:27:20.482 --> 00:27:22.812
Huh? This...

278
00:27:24.282 --> 00:27:25.282
This hurts.

279
00:27:25.283 --> 00:27:27.842
It's Man-Sik's laxative.
Laxative.

280
00:27:27.852 --> 00:27:29.382
He can't take a shit.

281
00:27:29.692 --> 00:27:31.482
So, you gave it to him.

282
00:27:31.562 --> 00:27:33.892
The watch was metal, not plastic.

283
00:27:34.562 --> 00:27:37.262
I could've died f I was hit directly.

284
00:27:51.482 --> 00:27:54.102
The watch wasn't found.

285
00:27:54.652 --> 00:27:56.512
Thanks to my long hair.

286
00:27:58.552 --> 00:28:00.312
He's the grandson of a big tycoon.

287
00:28:00.392 --> 00:28:03.152
No. He's the son of a congressman.

288
00:28:03.262 --> 00:28:05.361
I'm telling you he's the
grandson of a rich tycoon.

289
00:28:05.362 --> 00:28:09.492
Everyone argued about Seung-min's status.

290
00:28:09.792 --> 00:28:14.362
But they all agreed
he'd soon become stupid.

291
00:28:14.602 --> 00:28:16.262
Like the street musician.

292
00:28:23.682 --> 00:28:26.772
When I went to clean, his eyes were open.

293
00:28:27.152 --> 00:28:29.742
I told him how you (Miss
Lee) worried about him.

294
00:28:30.282 --> 00:28:33.752
He said he'll take you out on a date.

295
00:28:39.792 --> 00:28:43.022
Congratulations. 40 points.
40 points.

296
00:28:46.602 --> 00:28:50.602
When I pass, I'll prepare for university.

297
00:28:51.902 --> 00:28:54.802
I'm going to be a social worker.

298
00:28:54.912 --> 00:28:57.342
I'll work in a rehab for alcoholics.

299
00:28:57.482 --> 00:28:58.532
Alcohol.

300
00:28:58.842 --> 00:29:00.242
I know I can do it well.

301
00:29:00.312 --> 00:29:02.342
I won't hit like Spotty.

302
00:29:04.652 --> 00:29:06.282
Well, isn't that great?

303
00:29:07.792 --> 00:29:09.901
We took in a homeless alcoholic.

304
00:29:09.902 --> 00:29:13.452
Fed him and revived him. And what?

305
00:29:13.462 --> 00:29:15.722
You're just human trash,
abandoned by even your parents.

306
00:29:19.702 --> 00:29:21.432
A moron who didn't graduate middle school.

307
00:29:21.772 --> 00:29:24.053
Learn from another moron who
didn't graduate high school.

308
00:29:24.932 --> 00:29:26.881
And you'll become a social worker?

309
00:29:26.882 --> 00:29:29.662
And you won't hit like me?

310
00:29:33.952 --> 00:29:37.382
Who would license a psycho like you?

311
00:29:37.552 --> 00:29:40.812
You can't even become head
of a town, you bastard.

312
00:29:41.792 --> 00:29:46.012
And you. You seem to be
involved in everything.

313
00:29:46.512 --> 00:29:49.052
Go mind your own business, you asshole.

314
00:29:50.232 --> 00:29:52.752
I can't fucking tear this!

315
00:29:59.742 --> 00:30:01.792
Sometimes, there are those days.

316
00:30:02.412 --> 00:30:06.632
A strange day that makes
even normal people crazy.

317
00:30:07.332 --> 00:30:08.791
Hyun-Sun! Hyun-Sun!

318
00:30:08.792 --> 00:30:11.102
Some blame the weather.

319
00:30:11.552 --> 00:30:14.182
Some say the drug effect wore off.

320
00:30:15.902 --> 00:30:20.522
People here called it the curse of dusk.

321
00:30:38.042 --> 00:30:41.072
I was not an exception.

322
00:30:58.362 --> 00:30:59.362
Hey!

323
00:31:02.632 --> 00:31:03.732
What's wrong?

324
00:31:07.772 --> 00:31:10.152
Everyone's crazy.

325
00:31:10.452 --> 00:31:14.352
Now it really feels like
I'm in a mental hospital.

326
00:31:16.922 --> 00:31:18.982
Did they get released already?

327
00:31:20.052 --> 00:31:23.352
Yong had a fight so he's in
the Lily Room for 1 night.

328
00:31:23.362 --> 00:31:26.222
Man-sik's in treatment for
intestinal inflammation.

329
00:31:31.102 --> 00:31:34.862
I was here when I was young.

330
00:31:35.932 --> 00:31:37.602
When I was about 10 years old.

331
00:31:39.202 --> 00:31:42.102
For a young kid, I had to
vent out a lot of anger.

332
00:31:43.802 --> 00:31:47.502
Somehow I burned down
my dad's vacation home.

333
00:31:48.112 --> 00:31:54.312
But, after I went to the U.S., I had no such
urge. I even lost memory of being in Korea.

334
00:31:54.492 --> 00:31:57.582
But, I suddenly remembered it a while ago.

335
00:31:59.962 --> 00:32:01.762
I had to go somewhere.

336
00:32:04.062 --> 00:32:06.292
So, I gave everything he asked.

337
00:32:07.302 --> 00:32:09.532
But, I guess he wanted something else.

338
00:32:10.342 --> 00:32:12.902
He didn't put me here just to scare me.

339
00:32:13.712 --> 00:32:16.032
He wanted to really lock me in.

340
00:32:16.242 --> 00:32:18.182
So I can become totally stupid.

341
00:32:19.042 --> 00:32:23.772
Until I don't even know
who I am or why I was born.

342
00:32:25.822 --> 00:32:28.452
Like those patients in the hallway.

343
00:32:31.462 --> 00:32:33.222
That's my future.

344
00:32:34.562 --> 00:32:39.191
This isn't a prison. If you
behave, nobody bothers you.

345
00:32:39.192 --> 00:32:41.192
Time goes by pretty fast.

346
00:32:41.372 --> 00:32:46.832
Then, one day, you could go home.

347
00:32:48.942 --> 00:32:50.072
No.

348
00:32:50.582 --> 00:32:53.242
I have to get out now. No matter how.

349
00:32:53.852 --> 00:32:55.412
Don't have much time.

350
00:32:56.882 --> 00:32:58.572
And, that's driving me crazy.

351
00:33:07.092 --> 00:33:13.162
Hallelujah. Today's Bible
verse is Isaiah 43:18.

352
00:33:13.402 --> 00:33:17.842
"Forget the former things;
do not dwell on the past."

353
00:33:18.402 --> 00:33:19.662
Do you mean me?

354
00:33:21.002 --> 00:33:25.702
What? You mean Miss Lee's crazy soul too?

355
00:33:25.742 --> 00:33:27.612
You can forgive, too?

356
00:33:28.252 --> 00:33:30.342
Thank you. It'll be all right.

357
00:33:39.362 --> 00:33:41.852
Yong. What's that?

358
00:33:43.062 --> 00:33:44.062
That?

359
00:33:44.502 --> 00:33:46.232
It's from the boat yard.

360
00:33:46.772 --> 00:33:49.532
A boat yard? There was a boat yard?

361
00:33:49.602 --> 00:33:51.141
It was all right during winter.

362
00:33:51.142 --> 00:33:54.102
But, these days, those
parachuting kids drive me crazy.

363
00:33:59.742 --> 00:34:01.382
Hey! Where are you going?

364
00:34:03.302 --> 00:34:05.072
Stop! Han and Eun!

365
00:34:27.802 --> 00:34:31.801
Where are you going? Why
don't you go get him?

366
00:34:31.802 --> 00:34:34.302
Should we all go to the isolation room?

367
00:34:37.982 --> 00:34:39.042
Where are you going?

368
00:34:39.222 --> 00:34:41.021
How can I not go crazy with guys like that?

369
00:34:41.022 --> 00:34:43.592
You all want to go to the isolation room?

370
00:34:47.792 --> 00:34:49.582
Parachuting again today.

371
00:34:50.202 --> 00:34:52.022
- So ignorant.
- Ignorant.

372
00:34:52.632 --> 00:34:55.032
It's paragliding, not parachuting.

373
00:34:55.632 --> 00:34:57.792
This is why you have to go to the military.

374
00:34:59.842 --> 00:35:02.662
You'd think you've really
been to the military.

375
00:35:02.672 --> 00:35:05.442
I went crazy after being in the military.

376
00:35:20.762 --> 00:35:22.082
Hey, let's go.

377
00:35:29.972 --> 00:35:31.362
Open the door!

378
00:35:35.412 --> 00:35:38.142
Were we this insignificant?

379
00:35:38.482 --> 00:35:40.901
If the door's locked, we could run away.

380
00:35:40.902 --> 00:35:43.902
Shouldn't the hospital be in chaos?

381
00:35:44.082 --> 00:35:45.412
That? No?

382
00:35:45.712 --> 00:35:49.912
Hey Ddobyul, I told you not to pick that.
It's Spotty's, I told you, I did!

383
00:35:58.332 --> 00:35:59.922
What's wrong? Eat up!

384
00:36:00.102 --> 00:36:02.971
Since the door's closed, we
should eat without shame.

385
00:36:02.972 --> 00:36:04.592
What do we have to lose?

386
00:36:10.492 --> 00:36:15.272
Fortunately we didn't get any
beating or go to isolation.

387
00:36:15.282 --> 00:36:18.082
It was because Nurse CHOI was on duty.

388
00:36:19.252 --> 00:36:21.912
One thing has changed
since we were in the woods.

389
00:36:21.992 --> 00:36:25.852
Seung-min's been punching
he punchball for days.

390
00:36:26.392 --> 00:36:28.992
So, Man-sik moved over to me.

391
00:36:29.892 --> 00:36:32.692
- Ddobyul, stop.
- Teacher.

392
00:36:35.272 --> 00:36:38.432
I found out that I can
become a social worker.

393
00:36:38.872 --> 00:36:41.572
There're 20 jobs that Code
F citizens can't have.

394
00:36:41.672 --> 00:36:44.672
Social worker isn't one of them.

395
00:36:45.582 --> 00:36:46.812
That's great.

396
00:36:47.312 --> 00:36:48.642
So, I was thinking...

397
00:36:49.952 --> 00:36:52.472
Can we start studying again?

398
00:36:58.262 --> 00:37:00.522
Man-sik put it all back together.

399
00:37:08.302 --> 00:37:09.601
It's psycho drama time.

400
00:37:09.602 --> 00:37:11.732
Everyone, please gather
at the break room.

401
00:37:12.102 --> 00:37:13.662
Every one of you.

402
00:37:14.042 --> 00:37:15.042
Ddobyul.

403
00:37:21.552 --> 00:37:22.742
Ms. KIM Yeon-soon.

404
00:37:23.312 --> 00:37:25.781
Who do you want to play
the daughter, Hyun-sun?

405
00:37:25.782 --> 00:37:28.312
Hyun-sun? Hyun-sun.

406
00:37:37.432 --> 00:37:39.431
Hyun-Sun.

407
00:37:39.432 --> 00:37:40.562
Hyun-sun.

408
00:37:43.232 --> 00:37:44.902
Shit. Let me wash it out first.

409
00:37:47.912 --> 00:37:49.132
Ah, that stings.

410
00:37:54.652 --> 00:37:55.742
What's this?

411
00:37:56.282 --> 00:37:58.342
Going to post it on YouTube?

412
00:37:59.782 --> 00:38:02.682
Are you going to find her lost daughter?

413
00:38:02.692 --> 00:38:06.212
To treat wounds, the trauma.

414
00:38:06.322 --> 00:38:07.452
For treatment?

415
00:38:08.032 --> 00:38:11.732
Not for a thesis by an
old student in Ward 3?

416
00:38:11.792 --> 00:38:16.431
Don't think it would treat
one's trauma or wounds.

417
00:38:16.432 --> 00:38:19.632
If you don't want to do it,
just sit yourself over there.

418
00:38:21.912 --> 00:38:25.941
To me, it seems like she doesn't
want to meet her daughter.

419
00:38:25.942 --> 00:38:27.792
But, it's the opposite.

420
00:38:38.592 --> 00:38:43.492
Last night I met Hyun-Sun in my dreams.

421
00:38:46.032 --> 00:38:50.192
Hyun-sun says she can't forgive her Mom.

422
00:38:53.572 --> 00:38:58.012
Because she's never hated her.

423
00:39:00.882 --> 00:39:02.112
Hyun-sun.

424
00:39:04.002 --> 00:39:11.112
When the house was on fire
Hyun-Sun never woke up.

425
00:39:13.002 --> 00:39:21.002
Although the fire burned the blanket and her
body, she had no idea what had happened.

426
00:39:26.342 --> 00:39:30.932
She never once was afraid.

427
00:39:36.712 --> 00:39:38.112
Not once.

428
00:40:13.452 --> 00:40:17.392
Now, you'll feel better
when you wake up tomorrow.

429
00:40:29.942 --> 00:40:33.241
This place is too serious
for a mental hospital.

430
00:40:33.242 --> 00:40:35.242
What's good about being crazy?

431
00:40:36.942 --> 00:40:37.942
How about it?

432
00:40:38.342 --> 00:40:41.792
If I brighten up the mood,
you take off some penalty points?

433
00:40:43.382 --> 00:40:45.942
OK. if that's the case. Good!

434
00:41:21.792 --> 00:41:22.792
Bang!

435
00:42:15.172 --> 00:42:18.632
For that moment, we weren't crazy.

436
00:42:18.942 --> 00:42:20.842
We were just normal people.

437
00:42:22.382 --> 00:42:26.982
That day was Seung-min's
great gift to us all.

438
00:42:48.802 --> 00:42:50.802
I repeat. Patients leaving for vacation...

439
00:42:51.182 --> 00:42:54.672
Pigeon! Fly the pigeon.

440
00:42:55.452 --> 00:42:56.942
Where will it fly to?

441
00:43:25.382 --> 00:43:27.172
But, how did you know?

442
00:43:28.802 --> 00:43:32.801
Ah, Nurse Yoon Bora?

443
00:43:32.802 --> 00:43:35.202
No, Hyun-Sun's mom.

444
00:43:38.662 --> 00:43:39.882
I thought...

445
00:43:44.532 --> 00:43:46.592
maybe my Mom would be like that.

446
00:43:48.732 --> 00:43:50.502
After being separated since I was young,

447
00:43:51.312 --> 00:43:54.302
the reason that she never visited me.

448
00:43:56.242 --> 00:43:57.642
Because she was sorry.

449
00:43:58.182 --> 00:44:00.402
Afraid that she won't be forgiven.

450
00:44:31.442 --> 00:44:34.312
Then, you were sent here by your Dad?

451
00:44:38.052 --> 00:44:39.682
Kind of like that.

452
00:44:40.682 --> 00:44:43.282
I came back to Korea for my dad's funeral.

453
00:44:43.452 --> 00:44:44.942
Then, I was dragged in here.

454
00:44:46.462 --> 00:44:48.482
Where is it that you're trying to go to?

455
00:45:00.532 --> 00:45:01.731
SUANBO HOT SPRINGS FESTIVAL

456
00:45:01.732 --> 00:45:03.732
Hot springs festival?

457
00:45:10.482 --> 00:45:11.952
Annapurna?

458
00:45:19.962 --> 00:45:21.522
When you wake up,

459
00:45:22.932 --> 00:45:28.422
have you ever been afraid
that it'd still be nighttime?

460
00:45:57.632 --> 00:46:01.562
After some quiet time, Seung-min
finally caused trouble.

461
00:46:01.772 --> 00:46:04.232
The one who flew
the pigeon had flown in.

462
00:46:05.372 --> 00:46:07.092
- Get out of the way!
- Where are you going?

463
00:46:18.352 --> 00:46:19.612
Go back in!

464
00:46:26.612 --> 00:46:29.452
Seun-min! Seun-Min!

465
00:46:37.172 --> 00:46:39.662
Hey, isn't there a patient
named Ryu Seung-Min?

466
00:46:39.672 --> 00:46:41.541
You can't come in without a visitor's pass.

467
00:46:41.542 --> 00:46:44.251
I know everything. Where's RYU Seung-min?

468
00:46:44.252 --> 00:46:45.851
There's no such patient here.

469
00:46:45.852 --> 00:46:47.311
Don't bullshit me. I checked it all out.

470
00:46:47.312 --> 00:46:49.851
He's not crazy!
He shouldn't be here!

471
00:46:49.852 --> 00:46:51.042
He's not here!

472
00:46:51.852 --> 00:46:53.012
RYU Seung-min!

473
00:46:53.712 --> 00:46:57.851
Seung-Min, it's Young-Duk! Seung-Min!

474
00:46:57.852 --> 00:46:59.852
Over...
Seung-Min!!!

475
00:47:01.932 --> 00:47:03.022
Seung-min!

476
00:47:04.802 --> 00:47:08.321
Seung-min! RYU Seung-min!
I know you're here.

477
00:47:08.322 --> 00:47:10.322
Seung-Min, it's me Young-Duk!

478
00:47:12.322 --> 00:47:14.792
Seun-Min! LET GO OF ME.

479
00:47:25.802 --> 00:47:27.302
Hey, get him.

480
00:47:30.302 --> 00:47:34.802
Hey, you crazy bastard. Let me go! Fuck!

481
00:47:37.502 --> 00:47:40.802
Fuck, what are you looking at?

482
00:47:46.502 --> 00:47:49.932
Seung-Min was given
injections every 2 hours.

483
00:47:51.632 --> 00:47:55.132
People called it the 'stupid shot.'

484
00:48:40.932 --> 00:48:42.932
NURSE CHOI! OVER HERE!

485
00:48:45.632 --> 00:48:47.932
Ddobyul! Open your eyes!

486
00:48:48.932 --> 00:48:51.932
Hey! Anyone there?

487
00:48:52.732 --> 00:48:56.531
Hey, isn'y anyone there?
ISN'T ANYONE THERE?

488
00:48:56.532 --> 00:48:58.731
Ddobyul, don't be sick. Ddobyul, no.
Don't die.

489
00:48:58.732 --> 00:49:02.331
Over here!
Who is on duty today? Spotty?

490
00:49:02.332 --> 00:49:04.631
Is he playing cards again?

491
00:49:04.632 --> 00:49:08.632
He's burning up.
(A person's dying!)

492
00:49:08.802 --> 00:49:14.792
Spotty, you bastard! A person's dying.
A person's dying, you bastards!!

493
00:49:18.902 --> 00:49:22.501
Didn't you hear anything?
What's wrong with you?

494
00:49:22.502 --> 00:49:24.502
Don't stop the flow and deal.

495
00:49:26.702 --> 00:49:31.201
A person's dying! He's
dying, you bastards!!

496
00:49:31.202 --> 00:49:33.202
Wake up nurse Choi!

497
00:49:35.792 --> 00:49:37.301
What?

498
00:49:37.302 --> 00:49:41.102
Wake up nurse Choi, upstairs from you!
Break the window.

499
00:50:01.502 --> 00:50:04.192
Thank you, Nurse Yoon.
Aren't you going to deal?

500
00:50:19.802 --> 00:50:22.601
The window's up too high!

501
00:50:22.602 --> 00:50:24.602
Have Man-Sik do it!

502
00:50:36.202 --> 00:50:38.602
His arm can't get through.

503
00:50:38.902 --> 00:50:41.202
The laxative, Man-Sik's laxative!

504
00:51:14.302 --> 00:51:16.002
Who is it?

505
00:51:16.302 --> 00:51:21.792
Ddobyul's dying! Ddobyul's dying!
Ddobyul's dying!

506
00:51:34.002 --> 00:51:36.302
Ddobyul's dying!

507
00:51:38.502 --> 00:51:42.102
Please help him, please...

508
00:52:14.102 --> 00:52:17.102
So you broke my window with this?

509
00:52:26.302 --> 00:52:28.002
What is it? This time it's a radio?

510
00:52:34.002 --> 00:52:36.001
What about Seung-Min?

511
00:52:36.002 --> 00:52:38.001
He got an iridotomy.

512
00:52:38.002 --> 00:52:41.702
It might've been too late to
operate because of his cold.

513
00:52:43.702 --> 00:52:47.601
Then, is he all right now?

514
00:52:47.602 --> 00:52:52.612
The operation went well. But the eye
pressure's high so that'll affect him.

515
00:52:56.712 --> 00:52:59.251
It's called pigmentary
degeneration of the retina.

516
00:52:59.252 --> 00:53:01.692
Ryu Seun-Min was genetically
predisposed to it.

517
00:53:01.792 --> 00:53:06.692
The viewing angle gradually
becomes narrow, then it closes up.

518
00:53:06.992 --> 00:53:12.691
It's more dangerous when
the eye pressure goes up.

519
00:53:12.692 --> 00:53:17.892
So, he'll become blind?

520
00:53:19.792 --> 00:53:23.492
You said the operation went well.

521
00:53:23.792 --> 00:53:28.792
The operation was for glaucoma.
One of its complications.

522
00:53:29.692 --> 00:53:33.991
That's the problem. They say
it's already his 3rd operation.

523
00:53:33.992 --> 00:53:36.051
That means it could always recur.

524
00:53:36.052 --> 00:53:39.792
Then his remaining vision
can't be guaranteed.

525
00:53:42.492 --> 00:53:46.192
Don't have much time. And
it's driving me crazy.

526
00:53:48.092 --> 00:53:54.051
Sir, didn't you know already?

527
00:53:54.052 --> 00:53:56.051
I'm not a fortune teller.

528
00:53:56.052 --> 00:53:58.381
How would I know what his family
nor himself didn't tell me?

529
00:53:58.382 --> 00:54:03.282
You know why Seung-Min
is locked up in here.

530
00:54:03.992 --> 00:54:09.151
Lee Soo-Myung. You got it wrong. I...

531
00:54:09.152 --> 00:54:12.792
In a mental ward, there are two types.

532
00:54:14.792 --> 00:54:17.761
Those who are locked up
because they're crazy.

533
00:54:17.762 --> 00:54:20.191
Those who are locked up and become crazy.

534
00:54:20.192 --> 00:54:24.992
Which type Seung-Min is...
you really didn't know?

535
00:55:17.792 --> 00:55:19.591
Ddobyul.

536
00:55:19.592 --> 00:55:22.192
Seung-Min...

537
00:55:25.792 --> 00:55:27.902
Oppa's (I am) back.

538
00:55:40.802 --> 00:55:44.101
On a rainy day, Seun-Min
not only lost his sight...

539
00:55:44.102 --> 00:55:48.102
Words, expressions, anger, humor, energy.

540
00:55:48.702 --> 00:55:53.102
Even his specialty, his smiling eyes,

541
00:55:53.402 --> 00:55:56.102
he lost it all.

542
00:56:01.902 --> 00:56:05.902
Why bother hitting it when
it just hits him back?

543
00:56:33.702 --> 00:56:35.601
Ryu Seung-Min.

544
00:56:35.602 --> 00:56:37.792
Stop it and let's eat.

545
00:56:54.692 --> 00:56:55.792
Don't!

546
00:56:56.792 --> 00:56:58.392
Don't touch me.

547
00:57:46.592 --> 00:57:52.592
As expected, it finally happened.
But, much sooner than anticipated.

548
00:58:00.502 --> 00:58:04.201
On the 12th day since
Seung-Min lost his sight,

549
00:58:04.202 --> 00:58:06.792
finally his family member showed up.

550
00:58:20.792 --> 00:58:23.792
You're rejecting eye treatment?
Why is that?

551
00:58:23.992 --> 00:58:26.991
If they declare you blind I'll
send you to a better place.

552
00:58:26.992 --> 00:58:31.092
Florida or Hawaii. Tell me where.

553
00:58:35.402 --> 00:58:37.001
Why should I?

554
00:58:37.002 --> 00:58:41.002
I have two brothers in Korea.
Though we're not blood related.

555
00:58:41.792 --> 00:58:44.702
I'd really like to visit your house.

556
00:58:44.802 --> 00:58:47.202
So I can burn it down.

557
00:58:55.702 --> 00:58:57.602
It must be true.

558
00:59:04.702 --> 00:59:08.702
Why did dad leave you the damn stocks?

559
00:59:12.902 --> 00:59:14.801
He said he gave you everything you wanted.

560
00:59:14.802 --> 00:59:17.801
So why don't you let him out
when his eyes are like this?

561
00:59:17.802 --> 00:59:20.792
Did you get yourself a lawyer? In here?

562
00:59:20.802 --> 00:59:24.001
Why? Embarrassed to say it yourself?

563
00:59:24.002 --> 00:59:27.532
To take over the company
they lack 2% of stocks.

564
00:59:27.552 --> 00:59:29.602
Him and his older brother.

565
00:59:30.202 --> 00:59:33.552
Dad gave that damn 2% to me
so they don't fight over it.

566
00:59:33.792 --> 00:59:37.451
That's why I'm locked up in here.
So he can have the company.

567
00:59:37.452 --> 00:59:41.512
He's afraid I'll expose
him if I get outside.

568
00:59:42.792 --> 00:59:44.791
Isn't that why?

569
00:59:44.792 --> 00:59:47.092
Who'll believe crazy assholes?

570
00:59:48.002 --> 00:59:52.092
Hey, have you seen your
birth mother's face?

571
00:59:52.792 --> 00:59:54.901
If you haven't yet...

572
00:59:54.902 --> 00:59:57.902
you'll never know for
the rest of your life.

573
00:59:58.702 --> 00:59:59.702
Poor you.

574
01:00:10.752 --> 01:00:16.062
Oh. Jeh Young-Duk. He's
your friend (sunbae)?

575
01:00:16.262 --> 01:00:18.201
He came to see me.

576
01:00:18.202 --> 01:00:20.602
So, I decided to sponsor the team.

577
01:00:20.652 --> 01:00:24.602
Was it next week? They're
leaving for Annapurna?

578
01:00:35.602 --> 01:00:40.792
As I stayed by Seung-Min, Man-Sik
moved to the street musician.

579
01:00:58.192 --> 01:01:01.292
The nurses gave Seung-Min anti-depressants.

580
01:01:01.952 --> 01:01:04.792
Doesn't that mean he's suicidal?

581
01:01:07.092 --> 01:01:10.792
How much is it? That damned 2%.

582
01:01:12.092 --> 01:01:15.492
About $40 million.

583
01:01:16.912 --> 01:01:20.692
What? $40 million?

584
01:01:20.992 --> 01:01:23.691
While I was in the states,

585
01:01:23.692 --> 01:01:26.392
my old man hugely expanded the company.

586
01:01:29.792 --> 01:01:33.212
And you gave all that to that jerk?

587
01:01:33.512 --> 01:01:36.912
I told you, I had someplace to go.

588
01:01:37.612 --> 01:01:40.212
Before my eyes get worse.

589
01:01:41.712 --> 01:01:44.912
Are you going to outer space?

590
01:01:45.112 --> 01:01:50.212
Is there a place on earth that's
worth ditching $40 million?

591
01:01:58.002 --> 01:02:00.802
I want to go to Annapurna.

592
01:02:01.302 --> 01:02:06.302
I feel like I'm really
alive when I'm in the sky.

593
01:02:19.902 --> 01:02:22.102
Carried by the wind...

594
01:02:22.792 --> 01:02:26.702
I used to fly hundreds
of kilometers per day.

595
01:02:27.302 --> 01:02:30.302
Once, I flew up too high.

596
01:02:30.802 --> 01:02:34.702
Like Icarus who flew too near to the sun.

597
01:02:47.702 --> 01:02:52.202
Passed out, I was
floating around for hours.

598
01:02:58.102 --> 01:03:00.602
Then, I opened my eyes.

599
01:03:10.202 --> 01:03:13.351
At such a close range,

600
01:03:13.352 --> 01:03:16.352
I've never seen so many stars.

601
01:03:19.652 --> 01:03:22.352
A sea of stars.

602
01:03:23.052 --> 01:03:25.352
It was so beautiful.

603
01:03:27.392 --> 01:03:30.352
Enough to leave me breathless.

604
01:03:30.552 --> 01:03:32.752
Enough to want to die like that.

605
01:03:35.852 --> 01:03:38.802
My eyes could've got worse then.

606
01:03:39.502 --> 01:03:44.802
Since the eye pressure goes up
in high places with low pressure.

607
01:03:45.792 --> 01:03:49.102
The doctor said it was
dangerous to fly again.

608
01:03:49.402 --> 01:03:52.012
I was prohibited to fly.

609
01:03:53.792 --> 01:03:57.022
But I wanted to go back to the sky.

610
01:03:58.622 --> 01:04:01.502
Since my heart is still beating.

611
01:04:14.202 --> 01:04:16.402
Who are you?

612
01:04:17.112 --> 01:04:19.792
I often wondered.

613
01:04:20.292 --> 01:04:23.492
Who you really are.

614
01:04:24.792 --> 01:04:29.531
Not like those who hide
or those who just endure.

615
01:04:29.532 --> 01:04:34.802
The one who deals with your life.

616
01:04:37.702 --> 01:04:39.792
Do you have such a person in you?

617
01:04:57.492 --> 01:05:00.992
No, I don't.

618
01:05:02.892 --> 01:05:05.991
I don't.

619
01:05:05.992 --> 01:05:08.092
So what!

620
01:05:14.592 --> 01:05:17.691
The one who deals with my life?

621
01:05:17.692 --> 01:05:19.992
No such person existed.

622
01:05:20.492 --> 01:05:24.992
In my life, I was just a ghost.

623
01:05:25.192 --> 01:05:28.601
You killed her! Stabbing
scissors in her throat!

624
01:05:28.602 --> 01:05:32.602
Who says that? Who says that?

625
01:05:33.102 --> 01:05:35.602
Snap out of it!

626
01:05:35.802 --> 01:05:39.402
Don't!
Snap out of it!

627
01:06:05.352 --> 01:06:09.101
Listen up! Inside the
amusement park, Ward 3.

628
01:06:09.102 --> 01:06:11.102
To the fishing site, Ward 4.

629
01:06:11.302 --> 01:06:15.101
Ward 5 to the boat yard.
Go with the guardians.

630
01:06:15.102 --> 01:06:17.102
Move it, move it.

631
01:06:35.802 --> 01:06:39.401
Stay here a bit like this.

632
01:06:39.402 --> 01:06:40.701
Huh?

633
01:06:40.702 --> 01:06:42.792
I'll show you something funny.

634
01:06:43.992 --> 01:06:47.092
Hey Spotty, you fucking shit!

635
01:06:50.392 --> 01:06:52.591
Did that creep go mad?

636
01:06:52.592 --> 01:06:55.392
Guess you need more beating.
You do, you do.

637
01:07:14.392 --> 01:07:15.881
Can you see me?

638
01:07:15.882 --> 01:07:18.082
Well, not entirely.

639
01:07:19.102 --> 01:07:21.901
Maybe this much?

640
01:07:21.902 --> 01:07:25.101
Crazy bastard. You put on a show till now?

641
01:07:25.102 --> 01:07:27.601
Is that why you refused eye treatment?

642
01:07:27.602 --> 01:07:30.092
My acting was good, right?

643
01:07:31.602 --> 01:07:33.092
Let's go.

644
01:07:41.692 --> 01:07:43.092
Stop!

645
01:07:47.102 --> 01:07:48.902
Stop right there, bastards!

646
01:07:50.202 --> 01:07:53.792
Ryu Seung-Min and Lee Soo-Myung took off!

647
01:07:55.292 --> 01:07:58.092
Crazy bastards, come back here.

648
01:08:33.602 --> 01:08:36.801
Come out! Shoot me!

649
01:08:36.802 --> 01:08:39.501
Kill me! Try killing me!

650
01:08:39.502 --> 01:08:42.102
Shoot me in the heart, you bastards!!

651
01:08:49.102 --> 01:08:50.701
Wanna try?

652
01:08:50.702 --> 01:08:53.702
I can't even ride a bike well.
Oh, hey hey hey!

653
01:09:16.492 --> 01:09:18.792
Faster, faster!

654
01:09:19.792 --> 01:09:21.292
Just go!

655
01:09:49.792 --> 01:09:51.291
Over there.

656
01:09:51.292 --> 01:09:54.292
Slow down and get close to the right side.

657
01:10:00.802 --> 01:10:02.802
Want to come with me?

658
01:10:04.302 --> 01:10:05.792
No.

659
01:10:09.512 --> 01:10:11.792
What are you going to do now?

660
01:10:12.092 --> 01:10:13.991
What will I do?

661
01:10:13.992 --> 01:10:16.992
Go to Annapurna!
What?

662
01:10:18.592 --> 01:10:20.992
Hey!

663
01:10:44.102 --> 01:10:45.802
Out of my way!

664
01:10:46.502 --> 01:10:52.212
Everyone get out of my way! Out of my way!

665
01:11:33.712 --> 01:11:36.612
Had fun riding on the boat?

666
01:11:37.012 --> 01:11:39.801
From now on, you'll receive new treatment.

667
01:11:39.802 --> 01:11:42.301
You'll get several shock therapies.

668
01:11:42.302 --> 01:11:43.801
Shock therapy?

669
01:11:43.802 --> 01:11:47.501
It won't hurt, don't worry.
You'll be anesthetized.

670
01:11:47.502 --> 01:11:49.501
Because of you two,

671
01:11:49.502 --> 01:11:52.501
we can't have any more people getting hurt.

672
01:11:52.502 --> 01:11:55.701
From tomorrow, this week,
Ryu Seung-Min will go first.

673
01:11:55.702 --> 01:11:58.702
Next week, Lee Soo-Myung
will receive treatment.

674
01:12:01.702 --> 01:12:04.701
Soon, you'll all be good kids.

675
01:12:04.702 --> 01:12:07.792
So you won't get into trouble again, right?

676
01:12:22.392 --> 01:12:24.792
I heard you wrecked the boat.

677
01:12:26.952 --> 01:12:29.201
Why'd you get caught again?

678
01:12:29.202 --> 01:12:31.792
Forgot about the power of cell phones.

679
01:12:32.692 --> 01:12:37.792
Everyone was out to greet
me when I reached land.

680
01:12:39.192 --> 01:12:42.991
But, when I was coming out from the water,

681
01:12:42.992 --> 01:12:45.392
my underpants were gone.

682
01:12:46.092 --> 01:12:49.792
So I was nude with a plastic
bag hanging on my neck.

683
01:12:51.392 --> 01:12:53.091
After all that trouble,

684
01:12:53.092 --> 01:12:57.792
you got caught hanging a
plastic bag and your two balls.

685
01:13:00.102 --> 01:13:03.001
Can't you do anything right?

686
01:13:03.002 --> 01:13:05.202
Guess not.

687
01:13:07.002 --> 01:13:09.802
But what was your plan?

688
01:13:11.102 --> 01:13:12.801
About what?

689
01:13:12.802 --> 01:13:15.801
Where were you going to go?

690
01:13:15.802 --> 01:13:17.801
Suribong Peak.

691
01:13:17.802 --> 01:13:19.802
Why there?

692
01:13:20.402 --> 01:13:22.992
That's where the paraglider is.

693
01:13:24.092 --> 01:13:26.291
My friend will have put it there.

694
01:13:26.292 --> 01:13:28.492
If what Yong heard is right.

695
01:13:37.392 --> 01:13:39.201
But, the next day,

696
01:13:39.202 --> 01:13:44.202
Han got the shock therapy
first instead of Seung-Min.

697
01:13:45.002 --> 01:13:47.501
Soon, Han will reach a
state of enlightenment

698
01:13:47.502 --> 01:13:49.502
like the street musician.

699
01:13:50.402 --> 01:13:53.792
Of course, Seung-Min and I will, too.

700
01:13:53.992 --> 01:13:57.092
It's a pass, a pass!

701
01:13:59.192 --> 01:14:01.092
I passed, I passed!

702
01:14:05.592 --> 01:14:07.801
I passed.

703
01:14:07.802 --> 01:14:12.401
Eat up, Teacher. In the ward,
they'll take it all away.

704
01:14:12.402 --> 01:14:15.792
It's all thanks to you.
How could I ever repay you?

705
01:14:20.102 --> 01:14:23.291
The envelope truck comes on Fridays, right?

706
01:14:23.292 --> 01:14:25.791
Yeah. If there's nothing special.

707
01:14:25.792 --> 01:14:28.192
What time does it usually come?

708
01:14:28.792 --> 01:14:31.192
Around 2 to 3PM.

709
01:14:31.692 --> 01:14:36.192
Does the driver come alone
or does he have company?

710
01:14:36.292 --> 01:14:38.492
He's always alone.

711
01:14:40.592 --> 01:14:44.291
Please give Ddobyul a
ride in the laundry cart.

712
01:14:44.292 --> 01:14:48.292
He'll die or become stupid
if he's left in here.

713
01:14:48.792 --> 01:14:53.292
I'm not in a position to ask
such favors from the driver.

714
01:14:53.592 --> 01:14:57.592
But, only Ddobyul? Aren't you going?

715
01:15:01.502 --> 01:15:03.102
Me?

716
01:15:04.102 --> 01:15:06.801
You help me with my studies.

717
01:15:06.802 --> 01:15:09.101
And go to isolation because of Ddobyul.

718
01:15:09.102 --> 01:15:11.702
Why not do something for yourself?

719
01:15:19.912 --> 01:15:23.031
I saw many patients while staying here.

720
01:15:23.032 --> 01:15:26.002
But every time I see you, it's a bit...

721
01:15:27.252 --> 01:15:29.772
Why would such a person live like this?

722
01:15:31.022 --> 01:15:34.212
So, I asked Nurse CHOI when I
was going out to take the exam.

723
01:15:34.222 --> 01:15:36.382
About what Miss LEE was suffering from.

724
01:15:36.782 --> 01:15:39.782
He says you have escapism.

725
01:15:40.032 --> 01:15:43.332
I didn't understand it at the time.

726
01:15:43.432 --> 01:15:45.902
Did he mean escaping from the hospital?

727
01:15:46.232 --> 01:15:48.832
But, now, I think I do.

728
01:15:49.802 --> 01:15:54.902
It's escaping from the world.
And, from yourself.

729
01:16:03.052 --> 01:16:07.082
Teacher! Where you going?
Finish eating this!

730
01:16:14.132 --> 01:16:16.892
At 2p.m., the cleaner'll come to our room.

731
01:16:17.002 --> 01:16:20.192
Then, go down to parking lot
taking the elevator.

732
01:16:20.272 --> 01:16:22.411
Then, at 3p.m., the car will arrive.

733
01:16:22.412 --> 01:16:26.911
From there on, you can do your
best to get to Suribong Peak.

734
01:16:26.912 --> 01:16:28.912
Got that?

735
01:16:33.602 --> 01:16:39.301
So, the cleaner will come to the
room at 2PM to collect the sheets.

736
01:16:39.302 --> 01:16:41.801
Then, I hide in the laundry
cart, take the elevator,

737
01:16:41.802 --> 01:16:42.662
down to the parking lot.

738
01:16:42.663 --> 01:16:44.161
Then, the truck'll arrive at 3p.m.

739
01:16:44.162 --> 01:16:47.132
From there, I do my best
to get to Suribong Peak.

740
01:16:48.432 --> 01:16:51.232
Your eyes are still all right?

741
01:16:53.202 --> 01:16:56.072
It'll be fine until you lose all your hair.

742
01:16:57.472 --> 01:17:00.342
You can't ever come back this time.

743
01:17:02.012 --> 01:17:03.302
Mr. LEE Soo-myung.

744
01:17:05.182 --> 01:17:08.172
Nurse CHOI wants to see you.

745
01:17:39.482 --> 01:17:43.042
Your father passed away.

746
01:17:44.502 --> 01:17:47.742
Last Monday night, in his sleep.

747
01:17:49.362 --> 01:17:51.382
He had a bad heart.

748
01:17:52.732 --> 01:17:54.092
Did you know?

749
01:17:57.232 --> 01:18:01.722
The hospital recommended
surgery but he refused.

750
01:18:02.872 --> 01:18:06.002
It was his wish that
you don't come to the funeral.

751
01:18:07.372 --> 01:18:09.362
By his will, he was cremated.

752
01:18:10.582 --> 01:18:13.042
For you to stay here for life,

753
01:18:13.582 --> 01:18:15.912
he entrusted us all his assets.

754
01:18:17.852 --> 01:18:21.452
Your legal guardian is now your aunt.

755
01:18:51.722 --> 01:18:54.082
You'll soon get shock therapy.
Please get ready.

756
01:18:54.152 --> 01:18:55.961
Isn't it tomorrow?
It should be tomorrow.

757
01:18:55.962 --> 01:18:57.012
A change of schedule.

758
01:18:57.162 --> 01:18:59.452
The Director ordered it for today.

759
01:19:04.062 --> 01:19:05.722
Fuck!

760
01:19:06.072 --> 01:19:10.802
I'll kill you all!
Fuck!

761
01:19:11.242 --> 01:19:12.971
Shock therapy!
Shock therapy!

762
01:19:12.972 --> 01:19:15.942
Miss LEE can do it first.
Since it'll calm him down.

763
01:19:16.082 --> 01:19:17.082
LEE Soo-myung!

764
01:19:21.182 --> 01:19:22.612
Soo-myung.

765
01:19:25.852 --> 01:19:28.651
I am alone now.

766
01:19:28.652 --> 01:19:32.782
My Dad's dead and Seung-min will leave.

767
01:19:34.362 --> 01:19:37.852
Goodbye, Seung-min. Never come back.

768
01:19:41.132 --> 01:19:43.432
No need to worry about
becoming homeless.

769
01:19:44.272 --> 01:19:46.472
No need to worry about food.

770
01:19:47.912 --> 01:19:49.312
Safely,

771
01:19:50.282 --> 01:19:51.402
Protected,

772
01:19:53.182 --> 01:19:55.172
I'll live here until I die.

773
01:20:01.752 --> 01:20:03.982
Are you checking in
on your Mom often?

774
01:20:04.292 --> 01:20:06.622
Dinner at 7p.m.
Medicine at 9p.m.

775
01:20:07.322 --> 01:20:10.622
All right, how many times
do you have to tell me?

776
01:20:15.402 --> 01:20:17.962
Don't get lost in the books
and forget about it.

777
01:20:34.292 --> 01:20:37.522
Take good care of your Mom.
I'll be back on the first bus.

778
01:22:01.372 --> 01:22:04.742
Son, it's not your fault.

779
01:22:04.842 --> 01:22:08.142
Forget it.
Forget about it, son.

780
01:22:08.282 --> 01:22:11.092
Forget about it, son.
Don't!!

781
01:22:14.952 --> 01:22:18.792
Forget about it.
Forget it, son.

782
01:22:26.132 --> 01:22:27.292
Are you all right?

783
01:22:37.292 --> 01:22:39.132
The shock was very light.

784
01:22:39.142 --> 01:22:42.092
But, I was worried because
your state of dementia took long.

785
01:22:43.182 --> 01:22:45.712
I know you did it for Seung-min.

786
01:22:46.552 --> 01:22:52.052
But, you can't live his life for him.

787
01:22:56.702 --> 01:22:58.062
What time is it?

788
01:22:58.202 --> 01:22:59.432
2:40p.m.

789
01:22:59.972 --> 01:23:01.992
Seung-min would have left by now.

790
01:23:02.172 --> 01:23:05.062
Your friend worried a lot.

791
01:23:05.072 --> 01:23:09.202
He said he'll break my neck
if something happens to you.

792
01:23:10.242 --> 01:23:12.642
Couldn't get out because I was afraid.

793
01:23:24.262 --> 01:23:26.792
He'll feel really dizzy.
Take him back to the ward.

794
01:23:34.302 --> 01:23:36.132
Why are you here?

795
01:23:36.772 --> 01:23:39.572
- I have something to ask you.
- What?

796
01:23:40.412 --> 01:23:42.702
What'll you do
if your truck already left?

797
01:23:42.842 --> 01:23:45.312
Laun-dry!

798
01:23:58.692 --> 01:23:59.952
Think about it.

799
01:24:01.892 --> 01:24:03.792
Do you really want to
be here alone?

800
01:24:05.002 --> 01:24:06.492
Even when I'm not here?

801
01:24:12.912 --> 01:24:16.812
No.
Even if they give me $40 million.

802
01:24:33.832 --> 01:24:36.352
Bye, Ddobyul.

803
01:24:41.472 --> 01:24:43.132
Laun-dry!

804
01:25:14.372 --> 01:25:15.372
Hey!

805
01:25:19.842 --> 01:25:21.242
Why are there so much?

806
01:25:22.942 --> 01:25:24.142
Anyway,

807
01:25:25.042 --> 01:25:27.982
I heard you're preparing
for university?

808
01:25:28.752 --> 01:25:33.312
I guess we'll have a Ph.D. soon.

809
01:25:33.712 --> 01:25:35.792
I only graduated high school.

810
01:25:35.992 --> 01:25:38.822
Guess you won't talk to
an idiot like me now.

811
01:25:40.332 --> 01:25:42.121
What do you mean?

812
01:25:42.122 --> 01:25:45.792
Now that you're educated,
you tend to meddle around.

813
01:25:47.132 --> 01:25:48.332
You watch out.

814
01:25:48.932 --> 01:25:51.432
Before I chew you up.
Understand?

815
01:26:03.452 --> 01:26:05.002
What's with that Spotty creep?

816
01:26:05.022 --> 01:26:07.352
He's here to get the
envelopes for art class.

817
01:26:07.452 --> 01:26:10.442
- I'll see you next week.
- Yeah, let's have a drink later.

818
01:26:10.622 --> 01:26:13.252
PARKING GARAGE

819
01:26:22.772 --> 01:26:23.862
- What the...?
- Shut up!

820
01:26:25.072 --> 01:26:26.872
- Who are you guys?
- Shut up! Shut up!

821
01:26:39.702 --> 01:26:42.802
Where's the blind one and the crazy bitch?

822
01:26:43.022 --> 01:26:45.312
Probably went to the bathroom.
To take a shit?

823
01:26:47.792 --> 01:26:50.762
You! Go to the laundry room!
You! To the bathroom!

824
01:26:58.002 --> 01:26:59.132
I'll hit you!

825
01:27:21.192 --> 01:27:22.252
What's going on?

826
01:27:32.642 --> 01:27:34.302
Bastards, that's where they are.

827
01:27:45.802 --> 01:27:51.202
Nothing comes easily. Hold on tight.

828
01:27:51.402 --> 01:27:53.992
And I was so good to them!!

829
01:27:54.092 --> 01:27:55.292
Get out of the way!

830
01:28:08.212 --> 01:28:09.402
Stop!

831
01:28:09.812 --> 01:28:10.832
Hey, stop!

832
01:28:11.742 --> 01:28:13.342
Hey, stop!

833
01:28:14.212 --> 01:28:15.442
Hey, stop!

834
01:28:15.792 --> 01:28:19.342
Move, move!

835
01:28:30.762 --> 01:28:31.852
Get out!

836
01:28:45.582 --> 01:28:46.742
Hey, be careful!

837
01:28:51.022 --> 01:28:52.752
Hey, are you all right?

838
01:28:52.982 --> 01:28:55.382
I'm fine. Fine.
I'm a bit excited.

839
01:29:05.962 --> 01:29:07.592
Hey, it's Spotty!

840
01:29:07.672 --> 01:29:09.762
What fun would he have
without us?

841
01:29:26.762 --> 01:29:30.762
Hey, you crazy bastards! Stop the car now!

842
01:29:32.762 --> 01:29:36.002
I'm less crazy than you,
you crazy Spotty asshole!

843
01:29:44.002 --> 01:29:46.792
Hey, are you really crazy?

844
01:29:48.312 --> 01:29:49.802
Hey! Soo-myung!

845
01:29:51.642 --> 01:29:53.342
You crazy asshole. Say it again.

846
01:29:53.452 --> 01:29:55.112
What did you say?
You crazy bitch!

847
01:30:00.522 --> 01:30:01.791
Even now?

848
01:30:01.792 --> 01:30:02.952
Let me go!

849
01:30:03.592 --> 01:30:05.382
Aren't you going to stop even now? Huh?

850
01:30:06.582 --> 01:30:09.382
Aren't you going to stop even now?

851
01:30:40.532 --> 01:30:41.322
Are you all right?

852
01:30:41.462 --> 01:30:42.482
Yeah, I'm fine.

853
01:30:42.692 --> 01:30:44.462
Great hairstyle!

854
01:30:45.032 --> 01:30:45.862
Really?

855
01:30:45.962 --> 01:30:47.022
Yeah!

856
01:30:57.582 --> 01:31:01.642
- Going to the hospital?
- We can buy some time now.

857
01:31:03.112 --> 01:31:04.112
Let's go.

858
01:31:46.462 --> 01:31:47.462
It's a direct wind.

859
01:31:58.602 --> 01:32:00.632
If you go like this,

860
01:32:02.212 --> 01:32:03.542
you might die.

861
01:32:07.512 --> 01:32:08.812
Do you really have to go?

862
01:32:12.502 --> 01:32:16.491
I'm not trying to exchange
my life for a moment.

863
01:32:16.492 --> 01:32:18.962
To be truly myself in my time.

864
01:32:19.862 --> 01:32:21.492
That's life for me.

865
01:32:23.132 --> 01:32:24.602
I want to live.

866
01:32:28.102 --> 01:32:29.232
Soo-myung,

867
01:32:35.972 --> 01:32:37.702
Your time is now yours.

868
01:32:38.742 --> 01:32:40.142
Don't lose it any more.

869
01:32:48.792 --> 01:32:49.792
My friend.

870
01:32:52.962 --> 01:32:54.362
Aren't you going to say goodbye?

871
01:32:57.662 --> 01:32:58.992
I'll do it over there.

872
01:32:59.732 --> 01:33:01.362
Come running towards the light.

873
01:33:19.222 --> 01:33:21.012
Seung-min! Can you see?

874
01:33:22.092 --> 01:33:24.422
Yes! Of course!

875
01:33:40.932 --> 01:33:42.422
Bye, Seung-min!

876
01:33:49.482 --> 01:33:50.882
Goodbye, Seung-min!

877
01:33:54.382 --> 01:33:56.982
Goodbye! Seung-min!

878
01:33:59.822 --> 01:34:01.012
Seung-min!

879
01:34:05.932 --> 01:34:07.992
Go to Annapurna!

880
01:34:35.962 --> 01:34:37.292
Bye!

881
01:34:49.502 --> 01:34:51.642
Goodbye, Soo-myung.

882
01:34:53.792 --> 01:34:57.772
Seung-Min... goodbye.

883
01:35:19.232 --> 01:35:22.572
4 YEARS LATER
MENTAL HEALTH EVALUATION COMMITTEE

884
01:35:22.842 --> 01:35:27.272
Thank you for the story.
How's your panic disorder?

885
01:35:29.012 --> 01:35:30.711
If I tell you that
I get a haircut regularly,

886
01:35:30.712 --> 01:35:32.732
would that answer your question?

887
01:35:34.782 --> 01:35:38.742
You know, your legal guardian
is against your release?

888
01:35:39.302 --> 01:35:44.852
Aunt said my father's last wish was
to have me in the hospital for life.

889
01:35:45.152 --> 01:35:49.792
He also put money in the
trust only for hospital fees.

890
01:35:50.402 --> 01:35:54.792
Then you must resent your father a lot.

891
01:35:56.842 --> 01:35:58.392
Don't have to answer...

892
01:35:59.002 --> 01:36:03.792
Back then, back then I
didn't understand my father.

893
01:36:05.902 --> 01:36:10.172
But now, as a father
who had to leave behind

894
01:36:10.182 --> 01:36:12.642
his troubled child alone in the world,

895
01:36:14.392 --> 01:36:17.642
I feel that I might've done the same.

896
01:36:19.962 --> 01:36:21.722
Aiding and abetting suicide.

897
01:36:21.832 --> 01:36:24.592
- You weren't charged with it?
- No.

898
01:36:24.932 --> 01:36:29.632
The body was never found. Do you
accept Ryu Seung-Min's death?

899
01:36:33.712 --> 01:36:35.772
I don't think so.

900
01:36:36.792 --> 01:36:38.431
Some migratory birds fly

901
01:36:38.432 --> 01:36:41.172
halfway around the earth,
following the constellation.

902
01:36:41.482 --> 01:36:45.782
How far or where he flew off to,

903
01:36:46.322 --> 01:36:48.602
only he would know.

904
01:36:51.562 --> 01:36:55.152
Is there a reason for you
to tell us this story?

905
01:36:55.862 --> 01:36:58.192
To simply pass the evaluation,

906
01:36:58.262 --> 01:37:01.232
there was no need for such a long story.

907
01:37:05.732 --> 01:37:09.732
I myself needed a gliding site.

908
01:37:41.212 --> 01:37:43.632
Somewhere over the rainbow,

909
01:37:43.942 --> 01:37:46.441
I believe that unfulfilled
dreams of the past

910
01:37:46.442 --> 01:37:49.102
might be waiting for me.

911
01:37:52.252 --> 01:37:55.692
DEDICATED TO THE STRUGGLING YOUTH.
